  "features": [
    "HTTP/1 parser snapshots distinguish the first informational response from final headers and retain redirect-chain interval/final-hop start milestones.",
    "Tasklets expose measured interim/final response and redirect fields while publishing one entry for the original fetch URL.",
    "The Node HTTP request adapter now balances its internal socket cork on the next tick, preventing cork counts from growing across keep-alive requests and suppressing informational writes."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "The initial ordinary early-hints assertion failed on reused sockets. Controls traced an unmatched request cork; an ineffective ended-bit attempt was removed. Failed controls and diagnostic logs remain without passing credit.",
    "Complete protocol/cross-origin/redirect timing exposure, DNS/TLS/connection phases, HTTP/2/3, failure/data/file cases and partial-consumption accounting remain open under #873/#869.",
    "The seven-file unchanged corpus retains #874: 60 passes plus three process checks and one registered failure/failed file. This scope is not green.",
    "Previously excluded constructor/Deno regression files remain unverified and were not rerun; full Bun suite, #872 and Release/ASAN/all-platform coverage remain open under #66.",
    "Disk refusal and terminal cache cleanup are retained; both global-object producer outputs were preserved. Pickier has no errors and one existing quote-style warning after adjacent lint cleanup."
  ],
